  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1219 AM CST Wed Nov 25 2026\n\nRain has begun to move into the area tonight as a A strong \nshortwave moves across the region. The rain will continue \novernight through much of Wednesday. Rainfall amounts will vary, \nranging from just a few hundreds over the west to 1.5 to 2.0 \ninches in the east. The rain will end from west to east this\nafternoon into the evening hours. With the recent drought \nconditions and long duration of this rainfall, we do not expect \nany flooding concerns.\n\nExpect mainly dry and cool conditions on Thanksgiving day with \nhighs mostly in the low 50s. Temperatures will drop to around \nfreezing Thursday nigh across the entire area. The cool and dry \nconditions will continue through Friday, with a warmup on Saturday\nout ahead of another short wave that will bring more rain on \nSunday into Sunday evening. The next system does show some \ninstability, but is still several days out. Will continue to \nmonitor trends for potential strong to severe storms./15/",
